CrystalDK Beta 2.4.2 API

Quick Start

Basic pattern:

```lua
local CrystalDK = loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Daw1dk/CrystalDK/refs/heads/main/lua"))()

local Window = CrystalDK:CreateWindow({
    LoadingTitle = "CrystalDK",
    KeySystem = true,
    PermissionLevel = 0,
    ToggleUIKey = Enum.KeyCode.Y,
    MinimizeKey = Enum.KeyCode.T,
    ThemeCycleKey = Enum.KeyCode.L,
    BlurIntensity = 18,
    OpenFieldOfView = 35,
    OpenZoomDistance = 16,
})

local Main = Window:CreateTab("Main")

Main:CreateButton({
    Id = "hello_button",
    Title = "Hello",
    Subtitle = "Simple button",
    Callback = function()
        Window:SendNotification({
            Title = "CrystalDK",
            Subtitle = "Hello from the demo",
            Duration = 2,
        })
    end,
})
```

Common card fields

Most cards accept these fields:
- `Id`: stable card id / lookup key for `Window:GetValue`, rules, and `BringTo`.
- `Title`: main card title.
- `Subtitle`: secondary line under the title.
- `Default`: starting value for value-based cards.
- `Callback`: called when the card changes or is pressed.
- `Rules`: table of rule keys for this card.
- `RuleGroup`: named rule group or inline group source.

Rules can be supplied three ways:
- inside `Rules = { ... }`
- directly on the card config, like `RequirePermission = 2`
- by `RuleGroup = "GroupName"`

Most returned card objects expose:
- `Frame`
- `Get()`
- `Set(...)`

Cards

`CreateDivider({ Label })`
- Purpose: visual divider / section break.
- Return: no card object.

`CreateTitle({ Label | Title })`
- Purpose: titled section header.
- Return: no card object.

`CreateLabel({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Value | Default, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: static or live-updated text value card.
- Methods: `Set(value)`, `SetValue(value)`, `Get()`.

`CreateSlider({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Min, Max, Default, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: horizontal numeric slider.
- Methods: `Set(value)`, `Get()`.

`CreateStepper({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Min, Max, Default, Increment, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: numeric stepper with minus / plus buttons.
- Methods: `Set(value)`, `Get()`.

`CreateToggle({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Default, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: boolean on/off card.
- Methods: `Set(boolean)`, `Get()`.

`CreateButton({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Callback, Rules, RequireCooldown, CooldownDuration, ConfirmTitle, ConfirmSubtitle })`
- Purpose: action button card.
- Methods: `Press()`.
- Notes: `RequireCooldown` and `CooldownDuration` are button-specific config values, not generic rules.

`CreateImageButton({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Image | ImageId, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: action button with image badge.
- Methods: `SetImage(image)`, `Press()`.

`CreateProgressBar({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Default, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: horizontal progress card.
- Methods: `Set(percent)`, `Get()`.

`CreateCircleProgressBar({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Default, ProgressBarHeight, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: outside-mounted arc progress card.
- Methods: `Set(percent, instant?)`, `Get()`.
- Notes: the arc is mounted outside the left side of the card in a floating overlay layer, so it can overlap neighbouring cards without scroll-frame clipping.

`CreateDropdown({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Options, Default, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: single-select dropdown.
- `Options` can be raw values or `{ Label, Value, Callback }`.
- Methods: `Set(value)`, `Get()`.

`CreateGroupSelection({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Groups, Options, Default, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: grouped preset selector.
- `Groups` shape: `{ GroupName = { value1, value2, { Label, Value, Callback } } }`
- Internally builds a grouped dropdown.
- Methods: same as dropdown.

`CreateToggleDropdown({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Options, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: expandable multi-toggle list.
- `Options` shape: `{ { Label, Default, Callback } }`
- Methods: `Set(stateTable)`, `Get()`.

`CreateKnobSlider({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Knobs, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: one or more arc knobs.
- `Knobs` shape: `{ { Label, Min, Max, Default, Step | Increment, Callback } }`
- Methods: `Set(valuesTable)`, `Get()`.

`CreateKeybind({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Default, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: user-rebindable key card.
- Methods: `Set(keyCode)`, `Get()`.

`CreateMinimizeKeyinput(cfg)`
- Purpose: system key editor for the quick-select key.
- Methods: `Set(keyCode)`, `Get()`.

`CreateToggleUIKeyinput(cfg)`
- Purpose: system key editor for the main GUI toggle key.
- Methods: `Set(keyCode)`, `Get()`.

`CreateThemeCycleKeyinput(cfg)`
- Purpose: system key editor for the theme cycle key.
- Methods: `Set(keyCode)`, `Get()`.

`CreateInput({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Placeholder, Default, MaxLength, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: text input card.
- Methods: `Set(text)`, `Get()`, `Submit()`.

`CreateParagraph({ Title, Subtitle, Content })`
- Purpose: read-only paragraph / explanatory text.
- Methods: `Set(text)`, `Get()`.

`CreateRGBSelector({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Default, Callback })`
- Purpose: expandable RGB color picker.
- Methods: `Set(color3)`, `Get()`.

`CreateHSVSelector({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Default, Callback })`
- Purpose: expandable HSV color picker.
- Methods: `Set(color3)`, `Get()`.

`CreateColorSelection({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Options, Default, DefaultLabel, PerRow, Callback })`
- Purpose: palette / swatch selector.
- `Options` shape: `{ { Label, Color | Value } }`
- Methods: `Set(color3)`, `Get()`.

`CreateGradientSelector({ Id, Title, Subtitle, DefaultA, DefaultB, DefaultRotation, Callback })`
- Purpose: two-color gradient editor.
- Methods: `Set({ ColorA, ColorB, Rotation })`, `Get()`.
- `Get()` returns `{ ColorA, ColorB, Rotation, Sequence }`.

`CreateIconSelection({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Options, Default, PerRow, Callback })`
- Purpose: image / icon tile selector.
- `Options` shape: `{ { Label, Value, Image | ImageId, Callback } }`
- Methods: `Set(value)`, `Get()`.

`CreateStatusIndicator({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Default | Status, Percent, GradientColors, Callback })`
- Purpose: status card with gradient-driven color.
- Methods: `SetStatus(status, percent?)`, `Set(status, percent?)`, `Get()`.
- `Get()` returns `{ Status, Percent }`.

`CreateRepeatToggle({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Default, Interval | RepeatInterval, Callback, ToggleCallback, Rules })`
- Purpose: repeating toggle loop.
- `Callback` runs every interval while enabled.
- `ToggleCallback` runs when turned on/off.
- Methods: `Set(boolean)`, `Get()`, `IsRunning()`.

`CreateBanner({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Image | ImageId, Height, Tint, TintTransparency, Callback })`
- Purpose: large visual banner card.
- Methods: `SetImage(image)`, `Get()`.

`CreateLinkParagraph({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Content | Text, Links })`
- Purpose: paragraph with copyable / callback links.
- `Links` shape: `{ { Label, Url | Href | Value, Callback } }`
- Methods: `Set(text)`, `Get()`.

`CreateColor({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Default | Color, Callback })`
- Purpose: flat color fill card.
- Methods: `Set(color3)`, `Get()`.

`CreatePathInput({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Placeholder, Default, MaxLength, Callback, Rules })`
- Purpose: text input specialized for `game.Workspace.Part`-style paths.
- Methods: `Set(text)`, `Get()`, `Submit()`, `GetResolved()`.
- `GetResolved()` walks the path through descendants starting from `game`.

`CreateTable({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Columns, Rows })`
- Purpose: simple grid / row table.
- Methods: `SetRows(rows)`, `Get()`.

`CreateLineGraph({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Points | Values })`
- Purpose: line chart card.
- Methods: `SetPoints(points)`, `AddPoint(value)`, `Get()`.

`CreateSliderSelection({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Sliders | Options, Callback })`
- Purpose: compact vertical multi-slider card.
- `Sliders` shape: `{ { Label, Min, Max, Default | Value, Callback } }`
- Methods: `Set(index, value)`, `Get()`.

`CreateCardGrid({ Id, Title, Subtitle, Items, Columns, Callback })`
- Purpose: compact grid of action / toggle cells.
- `Items` shape: `{ { Label | Title, Type = "Toggle", Default, Callback } }`
- Methods: `Get()`.

Card Rules

Placement
- Put rules in `Rules = { ... }`
- Or directly on the card config
- Or register a group and use `RuleGroup = "Name"`

Value / input rules

`TrimSpace`
- Input-only.
- Removes whitespace from the entered string.

`OnlyNumber`
- Input-only.
- Keeps digits, minus, and decimal point.

`OnlyCharacter`
- Input-only.
- Keeps alphabetic characters only.

`OnlyPositive`
- Input-only.
- Removes a leading minus sign.

`OnlyNegative`
- Input-only.
- Forces a leading minus sign when text is present.

`RequireValidation`
- Input-only.
- Enables validation; pair with `ValidationPattern` or set it directly to a pattern string.

`ValidationPattern`
- Input-only.
- Luau pattern string used by `RequireValidation`.

`RandomizeValue`
- Value-based cards.
- Number form: symmetric range around the requested value.
- Table form: `{ Range | Amount, Min, Max, Round = false }`.

Behavior / action rules

`RequireHold`
- Button-style action cards.
- Requires hold before the action fires.

`HoldTime`
- Number of seconds for `RequireHold`.

`DynamicCallback`
- Function form.
- Signature: `function(windowState, value, cfg) -> callbackFunction`
- Lets one card swap its action at runtime.

`Debounce`
- Blocks rapid repeat actions.
- Number form: seconds.
- Table form: `{ Count, Window | Time }`.

`RequireDoubleClick`
- Requires two clicks within the threshold.
- Number form sets the threshold in seconds.

`Delay`
- Delays execution by N seconds after the action is accepted.

`Lock`
- Locks the card after a successful action.

`RequireConfirmation`
- Shows the built-in confirm modal before firing.
- Optional card config helpers: `ConfirmTitle`, `ConfirmSubtitle`.

`ClickCounter`
- Tracks sequential presses.
- Function form: `function(clickCount, windowState, value, cfg) -> callback`
- Table form: `{ [1] = cb1, [2] = cb2, ResetAfter = 3 }`

State / visibility / access rules

`RequireDependency`
- Accepted forms:
- string card id
- boolean
- function `function(windowState) -> boolean`
- table `{ Id, Equals, NotEquals }`
- array of requirement entries

`RequireState`
- Accepted forms:
- `Enum.HumanoidStateType`
- state-name string
- function `function(player, windowState) -> boolean`
- array of state requirements

`AutoDisable`
- If true, the card stays disabled and cannot be used.
- Accepted forms: boolean, function, string id, or `{ Id = "...", Equals = ... }`.

`RequirePermission`
- Requires `windowState.permission >= value`.

`GrantPermission`
- Usually used on `CreateInput`.
- Can be:
- `true` to parse the input text
- a number
- a string
- a table with `Level`, `Value`, or `Permission`

`PermissionBlur`
- Fully-covered permission mask overlay.
- Number = required permission level.
- This hides the card visually until that permission is granted.

`RequireCardVisible`
- Visibility gate.
- Accepted forms match `RequireDependency`.

`HiddenCard`
- Inverse visibility gate.
- Accepted forms match `RequireCardVisible`.

Navigation / copy / sync rules

`BindValue`
- Pushes a changed value into another card.
- Accepted forms:
- `"target_id"`
- `{ "id_a", "id_b" }`
- `{ Target = "target_id" }`

`CopyValue`
- Copies a value to the clipboard when the action succeeds.
- Accepted forms:
- function `function(value, windowState, cfg) -> text`
- string card id or literal text
- table `{ Text = "...", Id = "...", Value = anything }`

`BringTo`
- Navigates to a card or tab after the action succeeds.
- Accepted forms:
- `"card_id"`
- `{ Id = "card_id" }`
- `{ Tab = "Rules", Id = "target_card" }`

Live update / lifecycle rules

`RequireUpdate`
- Function only.
- Signature: `function(windowState, obj, cfg)`
- Runs every `RenderStepped`.

`OnClose`
- Function only.
- Signature at runtime: `function(windowState, cfg)`
- Runs when the main GUI closes.

Environment rules

`RequireKey`
- Accepted forms:
- `Enum.KeyCode.X`
- `"LeftShift"`
- `{ Key = Enum.KeyCode.LeftShift }`
- array of key requirements

`RequirePing`
- Number form: `<= value`
- Table form: `{ Max = n }` or `{ Min = n }`

`RequireRegion`
- Accepted forms:
- `Region3`
- table `{ Center | Position | Point = Vector3, Size | Extents = Vector3 }`
- function `function(rootPosition, player, windowState) -> boolean`

Visual rules

`Transition`
- Currently used by slider-style transitions.
- Number form sets the tween duration.
- Truthy non-number falls back to a short default transition.

`CardAccent`
- Adds a full-card gradient tint to the card shell and shifts the stroke toward the accent color.
- Accepted forms:
- `{ Color3, "tleft" | "tright" | "bleft" | "bright", intensity, onlyOnHover }`
- `{ Color = Color3, Side = "tright", Intensity = 0.9, OnlyOnHover = true }`
- `Side` chooses which corner/edge the gradient blooms from.
- If no color is supplied, the current theme accent color is used.

In-Depth Scenarios

1. Live mirror input

```lua
Tab:CreateLabel({
    Id = "mirror_label",
    Title = "Mirror",
    Value = "--",
})

Tab:CreateInput({
    Title = "Mirror Input",
    Rules = {
        TrimSpace = true,
        BindValue = "mirror_label",
    },
})
```

2. Admin-only action with confirm

```lua
Window:RegisterRuleGroup("AdminConfirm", {
    {RequirePermission = 2},
    {RequireConfirmation = true},
})

Tab:CreateButton({
    Title = "Delete Cache",
    RuleGroup = "AdminConfirm",
    Callback = function()
        print("admin action fired")
    end,
})
```

3. Command console

```lua
Window:RegisterCommand({
    ping = function()
        print("pong")
    end,
})

Tab:CreateInput({
    Title = "Console",
    Rules = {
        CommandInput = true,
        Commands = {
            localreset = function()
                print("local reset")
            end,
        },
    },
})
```

4. Region-gated action

```lua
local anchor = workspace.SpawnLocation.Position

Tab:CreateButton({
    Title = "Use Terminal",
    Rules = {
        RequireRegion = {
            Center = anchor,
            Size = Vector3.new(40, 20, 40),
        },
    },
    Callback = function()
        print("inside region")
    end,
})
```

5. Permission blur plus actual permission gate

```lua
Tab:CreateLabel({
    Title = "Admin Secret",
    Value = "Hidden tools",
    Rules = {
        PermissionBlur = 2,
    },
})

Tab:CreateButton({
    Title = "Admin Action",
    Rules = {
        RequirePermission = 2,
    },
    Callback = function()
        print("admin")
    end,
})
```

6. Live status card

```lua
Tab:CreateStatusIndicator({
    Id = "service_status",
    Title = "Service Status",
    Default = "Ready",
})

Window:SetCardStatus("service_status", "Syncing", 45)
Window:SetCardStatus("service_status", "Done", 100)
```

Window Settings

`CrystalDK:CreateWindow({ ... })`

Supported settings used by the current LIB:
- `LoadingTitle`: text shown on the key / intro surface.
- `KeySystem`: `true` enables the key gate.
- `PermissionLevel`: starting permission level.
- `ToggleUIKey`: default main toggle key. Default `Y`.
- `MinimizeKey`: default quick-select key. Default `T`.
- `ThemeCycleKey`: default theme key. Default `L`.
- `BlurIntensity`: blur size when the main GUI is open.
- `CameraTweenEnabled`: set `false` to disable the GUI camera tween.
- `OpenFieldOfView`: target FOV while the main GUI is open. Default `35`.
- `OpenZoomDistance`: target zoom distance while the main GUI is open. Default `16`.
- `CameraTweenTime`: open / close tween duration for the GUI camera presentation.
- `Commands`: global command map for `CommandInput`.
- `GlobalCardRules`: rules merged into every card.
- `RuleGroups`: named reusable rule groups.
- `FavouritesTabName`: custom name for the generated favourites tab.
- `OnClose`: window-level close callback.
- `PermissionKey`: function or table used to resolve permission from a raw key.
- `SuffixProfiles`: suffix-based profiles applied after successful key validation.
- `KeySettings`: key-system settings table.

`KeySettings`
- Supported fields actually consumed by the current LIB:
- `Subtitle`: placeholder text in the key input.
- `Keys`: array of valid keys.

`KeySettings.Keys` entry forms
- raw string: `"MyKey"`
- table: `{ Key = "MyKey", Permission = 2, Suffixes = {"dev"}, RequireSuffix = true }`
- accepted aliases for the key text: `Key`, `Value`, `Name`
- permission aliases: `Permission`, `Level`

`PermissionKey`
- Function form:

```lua
PermissionKey = function(rawKey, suffix, entry, windowState)
    return 2
end
```

- Table form:

```lua
PermissionKey = {
    ["MyKey"] = 1,
    ["MyKey:developer"] = 3,
}
```

`SuffixProfiles`
- Table form:

```lua
SuffixProfiles = {
    developer = {
        Permission = 3,
        OnLoad = function(windowObj, windowState, profile)
        end,
    },
}
```

- Function form:

```lua
SuffixProfiles = {
    developer = function(windowObj, windowState)
    end,
}
```

Window / Misc API

`Window:GetValue(id)`
- Returns the current stored value for a card id.

`Window:GetCard(id)`
- Returns the created card object for a card id when you need the raw object.

`Window:SetCard(id, ...)`
- Calls `:Set(...)` or `:SetValue(...)` on a card by id.

`Window:SetCardStatus(id, status, percent)`
- Calls `:SetStatus(status, percent)` on a card by id.

`Window:CallCard(id, methodName, ...)`
- Calls any card method by id and returns its result.

`Window:SetPermissionLevel(level)`
- Sets current permission and refreshes permission masks / layout.

`Window:GetPermissionLevel()`
- Returns the current permission level.

`Window:GetKeySuffix()`
- Returns the active key suffix or `nil`.

`Window:SetBlurIntensity(amount)`
- Changes the live open-GUI blur amount.

`Window:BringToCard(target)`
- Target forms:
- `"card_id"`
- `{ Id = "card_id" }`
- `{ Tab = "Rules", Id = "card_id" }`

`Window:FocusSearch()`
- Opens the GUI if needed and focuses the built-in search box.

`Window:RegisterRuleGroup(name, rules)`
- Registers or replaces a reusable rule group.

`Window:CycleTheme()`
- Rotates the active built-in theme.

`Window:SendNotification({ Title, Subtitle, Duration })`
- Shows the built-in toast.

`Window:RegisterCommand(name, callback)`
- Registers one command.

`Window:RegisterCommand({ commandA = fnA, commandB = fnB })`
- Registers many commands at once.

`Window:Tab(name)`
- Cached tab accessor. Creates the tab the first time, then returns the same tab object on later calls.

`Window:CreateTab(name)`
- Creates a tab and returns the cached tab object.

`Window.State`
- Exposes live internal state, including:
- `permission`
- `values`
- `commands`
- `toggleUIKey`
- `minimizeKey`
- `themeCycleKey`
- `blurIntensity`
- `suffix`
- `keyProfile`
